# taf.ul.kpi_selector

[![Documentation](https://docs.taf.ute.nsn-rdnet.net/projects/taf-ul-kpi_selector/badge/)][1]
[![Requirements](https://taf.wrgitlab-pages.int.net.nokia.com/miscellaneous/static-badges/requirements.svg)](requirements/base.txt)
[![build status](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/taf.ul.kpi_selector/badges/main/pipeline.svg)][2]
[![coverage report](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/taf.ul.kpi_selector/badges/main/coverage.svg)][2]
[![latest release](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/taf.ul.kpi_selector/-/badges/release.svg)][3]


taf.ul.kpi_selector library

Gets timeouts for operations depending on testline setup.

Supported operations:

* bts_cold_startup
* site_reset
* sw_update
* sw_activation
* sw_rollback
* snapshot_collection
* rf_lock
* rf_unlock
* reset_rf
* cell_lock
* cell_unlock
* cell_block
* cell_unblock
* reset_cu
* gsm_rat_reset
* wcdma_rat_reset
* lte_rat_reset
* nr_rat_reset


## Supported Python versions

Library should work properly with Python versions specified within
`python_requires` option in [setup.py](setup.py).

## Installation

Generic library installation process is described in [TAF user guide][4].

## Usage
First, import `kpi_selector` class and create it's instance in Robot file:

```robot
*** Settings ***
Library     taf.ul.kpi_selector  WITH NAME  kpi_selector
```

Then use `get_kpi` with chosen operation. This allows to get whole dictionary with timeout, operation name,
start & end point of operation and requirement reference from Gates.

```robot
*** Test Cases ***
Exemplary test case
    ${kpi_reset_site}=  kpi_selector.get_kpi
    ...                 operation=site_reset
```

If you wish to have `ran_type` different than default `Classical`, you can specify it:

```robot
*** Test Cases ***
Exemplary test case
    ${kpi_reset_site}=  kpi_selector.get_kpi
    ...                 operation=site_reset
    ...                 ran_type=Cloud
```

Example of return value:

```robot
{'End point': 'First cell up',
 'Operation': 'RF Reset',
 'Requirement': 'OM_GEN_SFS_PERF_CAP.19195',
 'Start point': 'Last cell down',
 'Timeout': 588}
```

To get only timeout value:

```robot
${kpi_reset_site['Timeout']}
```

